<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90187" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προστρέπω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turn towards</i>, esp. <i>towards a god</i> as a
			suppliant, <i>approach with prayer, supplicate</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοσαῦτά σ᾽, ὦ Ζεῦ, προστρέπω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					831
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. pers. et inf., <i>entreat</i> one to
			do, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή μ᾽ ἀτιμάσῃς . . , ὧν </span>( 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τούτων ἃ</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> σε προστρέπω φράσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OC</u>
					50
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. rei et inf., <i>pray that . . </i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλέσθαι πρόστρεπ᾽ Ἀργείων χθόνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					1195
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, with aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσετραπόμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hom.
					<u>Epigr.</u>
					15.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δῶμα, δόμους</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				205
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν Διὸς . . Ἐργάνην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					844
				</span></i>
			: in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cleom.</u>
				39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				15.21
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>reverence, celebrate</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1117a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>approach</i> (as an enemy), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰαωλκὸν πολεμίᾳ χερὶ προστραπών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					4.55c
				</span></i>
			odd. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>make a matter of supplication, appeal to</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ παθόντος προστρεπομένου τὴν πάθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					866b
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
